        "vins_title": "Jura wines",
        "vins_p1": "In the west of Franche-Comté, on the hillsides that border the plain, lies a small wine region with highly distinctive wines, grouped under the Jura appellation. Five grape varieties are grown there: Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, well known elsewhere, and three that are emblematic of the region: Savagnin, Poulsard and Trousseau.",
        "vins_p2": "Seven wines tell the story of this vineyard well, from aperitif to dessert: Crémant to begin, Macvin to finish. They come from winegrowers and wine cooperatives, and go naturally with the local cooking.",
        "voile_title": "Topped up or under a veil: the key to the region's white wines",
        "voile_text": "In the barrel, wine slowly evaporates. The winemaker then has two choices. If the barrel is regularly topped up, the wine stays protected from the air: this is called <em>ouillage</em>, and it gives fresh, floral, mineral whites. If the level is left to drop, a thin veil of yeast forms on the surface, protects the wine and slowly transforms it: it develops notes of walnut, spice and dried fruit, the famous “goût de jaune”. This is the secret of vin jaune, which spends more than six years under its veil, and of the wines known as “typé”.",
        ".lbl-secret": "Its secret", ".lbl-taste": "On the palate", ".lbl-table": "At the table", ".lbl-enjoy": "How to enjoy it",
        "w1_tag": "Sparkling · white",
        "w1_secret": "The bubbles of the Franche-Comté vineyards, made as in Champagne by a second fermentation in the bottle: the traditional method. The appellation has existed since 1995.",
        "w1_taste": "Fine bubbles, a fresh and lively palate, notes of white fruit and citrus.",
        "w1_table": "As an aperitif, with cubes of young Comté or Comté gougères.",
        "w1_serve": "Serve at 6–8 °C",
        "w2_tag": "Dry white · topped up (ouillé)",
        "w2_secret": "The world's most famous white grape takes on a particular accent here, on marl and limestone soils. <em>Ouillé</em>, that is, protected from the air throughout its ageing, it keeps all its freshness.",
        "w2_taste": "Dry, round and mineral, with notes of white flowers.",
        "w2_table": "Trout, Comté fondue, Comté aged a few months.",
        "w2_serve": "Serve at 10–12 °C",
        "w3_tag": "Dry white · typé, aged under a veil",
        "w3_secret": "The region's great white grape, the one used for vin jaune. In its “typé” style, it ages under a veil, without topping up, and it is this veil of yeast that gives it its very particular taste.",
        "w3_taste": "Dry and broad, with notes of fresh walnut, gentle spice and dried fruit. A long finish that surprises with the first sip.",
        "w3_table": "The natural partner of aged Comté, baked Mont d'Or, fondue and creamy dishes such as chicken with vin jaune.",
        "w3_serve": "Serve at 12–14 °C",
        "w4_name": "Jura rosé",
        "w4_tag": "Dry rosé",
        "w4_secret": "A rosé from the region in a classic style, chosen for its lightness and fruit, to be drunk young.",
        "w4_taste": "Dry, light and fruity, with notes of small red berries.",
        "w4_table": "Cured meats, mixed salads, Montbéliard sausage.",
        "w4_serve": "Serve at 8–10 °C",
        "w5_tag": "Light red · also called Ploussard",
        "w5_secret": "The red that people mistake for a rosé. Its grapes have thin skins with few pigments, which gives the wine a very pale, almost translucent colour, often compared to coral. The village of Pupillin, which has made it its speciality, calls itself the capital of Ploussard.",
        "w5_taste": "Light, with very soft tannins and notes of small red berries.",
        "w5_table": "Morteau sausage, cured meats, poultry. Serve it slightly chilled.",
        "w5_serve": "Serve at 12–14 °C",
        "w6_tag": "Red",
        "w6_secret": "Deeper in colour and more structured than Poulsard, it remains an elegant red. The village of Montigny-lès-Arsures, near Arbois, calls itself its capital.",
        "w6_taste": "Ripe red and black fruit, a hint of pepper, a round palate.",
        "w6_table": "Morteau sausage with lentils, grilled meat, game.",
        "w6_serve": "Serve at 14–16 °C",
        "w7_tag": "White fortified wine (vin de liqueur) · 16 to 22% vol.",
        "w7_secret": "The fermentation of the grape juice is stopped, just as it begins, by adding grape marc brandy from the same estate; the blend is then aged for at least a year in oak barrels. Macvin thus keeps the sugar and fruit of the grape. An old tradition that became an appellation in 1991.",
        "w7_taste": "Sweet and lively at the same time: grape, dried fruit, honey, with the brandy well integrated.",
        "w7_table": "Well chilled, as an aperitif or with dessert: melon, foie gras, walnut desserts.",
        "w7_serve": "Serve at 8–10 °C",
        "legal_1": TERROIR_LEGAL_FR + " (Alcohol abuse is dangerous for your health; please drink in moderation.)",
